- **Major — disabling the observer also prevents journal expiry.** [ingestion_observer.go:72](/var/folders/n0/yx26c20j4y5b0597zqpc5kzh0000gn/T/codex-gate-tree.wAambj/tree/slack-full/adapter/ingestion_observer.go:72): With `SLACK_INGESTION_OBSERVER_DISABLED=1`, deliveries still enter the journal, but nothing marks them ingested or alerted. Retention therefore treats every handoff as unresolved and permanently pins its day and all later segments. One delivered receipt is enough to defeat configured retention. Once accumulated segments exceed 64 MiB, reconstruction rejects them, so re-enabling the observer cannot recover without manual cleanup. Propagate the disabled state into a bounded retention policy, and cover expiry and re-enabling with a regression test.

Tests: **not run (sandbox)**. [Committed evidence](/var/folders/n0/yx26c20j4y5b0597zqpc5kzh0000gn/T/codex-gate-tree.wAambj/tree/assets/pr-evidence/gp-41p6/round-2/test-results.json) reports passing focused ingestion tests, adapter/CLI race suites, vet, and Python tests; it does not cover disabled-observer retention.

